  "slots": {
    "composition_parti": {
      "binding": "specified",
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "high",
      "judgment": false,
      "rule": "The elevation is irregular and additive except across the composed gatehouse entrance range, where a centred arch, flanking turrets and an oriel establish a local three-part symmetry that does not extend around the corner. This is Tudor's own proportional_system.symmetry ('near-symmetrical') and bay_rhythm ('Irregular and additive except across the composed entrance range... Windows are placed where rooms need them'), and it directly overrides an incorrectly inherited strict-bilateral-symmetry binding that reached this node only through italian-renaissance, a lineage edge Tudor's own text says is 'confined to ornament... No Tudor building is proportioned classically.' A whole-elevation classical symmetry claim has no business governing a style whose own source explicitly denies classical proportion.",
      "note": "CASCADE FIX. Before this binding, composition_parti resolved to antique-classical's 'strict-bilateral-symmetry' (forbidding picturesque-asymmetrical outright), reached via tudor's weight-0.2 references-only lineage to italian-renaissance ('transmission is real but confined to ornament'). That is architecturally wrong: Tudor's own proportional_system.symmetry is 'near-symmetrical', not strict-bilateral, and its own bay_rhythm text is explicit that the plan is irregular and additive outside the entrance range. Fixed here rather than on any ancestor kit, per WP-4.2 guidance.",
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "picturesque-asymmetrical",
          "status": "canonical",
          "note": "The whole-house condition: courtyard ranges laid out as function requires, with windows placed where rooms need them rather than to a facade grid."
        },
        {
          "id": "strict-bilateral-symmetry",
          "status": "atypical",
          "note": "Achieved only locally, at the composed gatehouse entrance range (centred arch, flanking turrets, oriel above) -- and even there it 'does not extend around the corner' (own proportional_system.bay_rhythm). Treating the whole elevation as strictly symmetrical is the mistake this binding corrects."
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        "tudor.json proportional_system.symmetry and bay_rhythm"
      ],
      "group": "massing-and-roof"
    },
