      "binding": "specified",
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "high",
      "judgment": false,
      "rule": "Crenellated parapets, corner turrets and gatehouse towers are used as non-defensive display, never as working military apparatus -- battlements you cannot fight from. Arrow loops, machicolation and portcullis grooves are false archaeology and forbidden.",
